":"openalex:W7172434380","title":"Pregnancy promotes tumor metastasis through adenosine-induced immunosuppressive neutrophils in pre-metastatic microenvironment","authors":["Chen Chen","Jiahong Shi","Yutiantian Lei","Qian Wang","Peihai Cao","Dairu Hou","Mengdi Huang","Ruiying Wang","Qiuyu Mu","Tingting Lv","Rui Jia","Mingjun Si","Dingge Jiang","Lei Li","Zhixuan Cai","Yakun Huang","Jiahao Sun","Lianying Jiao","Zhengtao Xiao","Yuhan Li","Binxian Wang","Shan Huang","Wenqian Du","Lu Bai","Jinlu Ma","Suxia Han","Baojun Zhang","Chen Lin","Hui Guo","Xiangjiao Meng","Yuzhu Hou"],"published":"2026-08-04","year":2026,"month":8,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-76158-3","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7172438828","title":"Technoeconomic competitiveness of small modular reactors across U.S. power and industrial sectors","authors":["Marisol Garrouste","Brendan Kochunas","Max Vanatta","Michael Craig"],"published":"2026-08-04","year":2026,"month":8,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-76077-3","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7172461743","title":"Publisher Correction: CFTR mediates Cl- transport in osteocytes to sustain cell viability and skeletal homeostasis","authors":["Peijie Hu","Wanting Du","Muyan Chu","Junjiang Chen","Xiaotian Zhang","Ziyi Chen","Jun Hu","Lei Qin","Wayne Lee","Jinghui Guo","Hui Chen","Ruiyao Xu","Xiaojun Cai","Xiaohua Jiang","Hsiao Chang Chan","Ling Qin","Jiankun Xu","Ye Chun Ruan"],"published":"2026-08-04","year":2026,"month":8,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-76088-0","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7172526094","title":"Trajectory forecasting lifts the femtosecond ceiling in molecular simulation","authors":["Seyed Mohamad Moosavi"],"published":"2026-08-05","year":2026,"month":8,"has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":["Sim2Real","RobotLearn","Climate"],"venue":"Nature Machine Intelligence","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7172542015","title":"SaLon3R: Structure-Aware Long-Term Feedforward 3D Reconstruction from Unposed Images","authors":["Jiaxin Guo","Tongfan Guan","Wenzhen Dong","Wenzhao Zheng","Wenting Wang","Yue Wang","Yeung Yam","Yun-Hui Liu"],"published":"2026-08-01","year":2026,"month":8,"pdf_url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s11263-026-02965-2.pdf","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":["NeRF","3DRecon"],"_topics":["3d gaussian splatting","long-term video reconstruction"],"venue":"IJCV","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0,"summary_zh":"本文提出SaLon3R，解决长期视频序列中3D重建冗余和几何不一致问题。方法引入紧凑锚点原语替代像素高斯，通过可微显眼高斯量化过程保证紧凑表示。","summary_en":"This paper proposes SaLon3R to address redundancy and geometric inconsistencies in long-term video 3D reconstruction. The method introduces compact anchor primitives replacing per-pixel Gaussians, ensured by a differentiable, saliency-aware Gaussian quantization process.","insights":["创新点：提出紧凑锚点原语解决冗余问题","方法亮点：引入可微显眼高斯量化过程","关键发现：显著提高长期视频3D重建质量"],"insights_en":["Novelty: Proposes compact anchor primitives to solve redundancy issues","Method highlight: Introduces a differentiable, saliency-aware Gaussian quantization process","Key finding: Significantly improves the quality of long-term video 3D reconstruction"],"abstract":"Abstract Recent advances in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) have enabled feed-forward, on-the-fly reconstruction of sequential input views. However, existing methods often predict per-pixel Gaussians and combine Gaussians from all views as the scene representation, leading to substantial redundancies and geometric inconsistencies in long-duration video sequences. To address this, we propose SaLon3R , a novel framework for S tructure- a ware, Lon g-term 3 DGS R econstruction. Our method eliminates redundancy by introducing compact anchor primitives as a replacement for per-pixel Gaussians. These primitives are derived through a differentiable, saliency-aware Gaussian quantization process designed to preserve fidelity while ensuring a compact representation. Specifically, a foundational 3D reconstruction model is employed to predict a saliency map encoding regional geometric complexity. Guided by this saliency map, we compress redundant Gaussian primitives into compact anchors by prioritizing high-complexity regions. Furthermore, we introduce a 3D Point Transformer to overcome geometric inconsistencies caused by long-term accumulative errors. It refines attributes and saliency of the anchor primitives leveraging the learned spatial structural priors in 3D space. Without known camera parameters or test-time optimization, our approach effectively prunes the redundant 3DGS and resolves artifacts in a single feed-forward pass. Experiments on multiple datasets demonstrate our approach outperform state-of-the-arts on both novel view synthesis and depth estimation, while exhibiting superior efficiency ( $$&gt;\\!$$ <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mml:mrow> <mml:mo>&gt;</mml:mo> <mml:mspace/> </mml:mrow> </mml:math> 10 ), robustness, and generalization ability for long-term feed-forward Gaussian reconstruction."},{"id":"openalex:W7172483046","title":"First poo transplant to treat food allergy in people has ‘exciting’ results","authors":["Edward Chen"],"published":"2026-08-05","year":2026,"month":8,"has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7172483687","title":"Editorial Expression of Concern: Tumour exosome integrins determine organotropic metastasis","authors":["Ayuko Hoshino","Bruno Costa-Silva","Tang‐Long Shen",